defconfig: enable HDMI RX and the USB HID gadget

The BSP's rtd129x_bpi_defconfig leaves both of these off:

  CONFIG_RTK_HDMIRX          the V4L2 capture driver; the whole project
                             depends on it
  CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_F_HID  kvmd's otg HID (keyboard / mouse)

During debugging we also enabled CONFIG_DEVMEM=y with STRICT_DEVMEM off, so
tools/rdreg.py could read and write the pinmux and HDMI RX registers
directly. **That setting is deliberately not kept here** -- a KVM sits on a
management network and holds the console of somebody else's machine, so a
shipping image should not leave an unrestricted /dev/mem behind.

To make a debug build, layer this on top of this patch:

  CONFIG_DEVMEM=y
  # CONFIG_STRICT_DEVMEM is not set

Routine pinmux verification does not need /dev/mem: whether the source
negotiated 1080p60 (hdmirx-info's Width/Height/Fps) is sufficient proof that
DDC works.

---

diff --git a/linux-rtk/arch/arm64/configs/rtd129x_bpi_defconfig b/linux-rtk/arch/arm64/configs/rtd129x_bpi_defconfig
index 1103b93a7..d47446846 100644
--- a/linux-rtk/arch/arm64/configs/rtd129x_bpi_defconfig
+++ b/linux-rtk/arch/arm64/configs/rtd129x_bpi_defconfig
@@ -3090,7 +3090,7 @@ CONFIG_VIDEO_EM28XX_RC=m
 CONFIG_RTK_HDMITX=y
 # CONFIG_RTK_HDCP_1x is not set
 # CONFIG_RTK_HDCP_1x_TEE is not set
-# CONFIG_RTK_HDMIRX is not set
+CONFIG_RTK_HDMIRX=y
 # CONFIG_RTK_HDCP1x_REPEATER is not set
 # CONFIG_RTK_HDCPRX_1P4_TEE is not set
 # CONFIG_RTK_HDCPRX_2P2 is not set
@@ -4050,7 +4050,7 @@ CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_UEVENT=y
 # CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_F_UAC1 is not set
 # CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_F_UAC2 is not set
 CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_F_MIDI=y
-# CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_F_HID is not set
+CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_F_HID=y
 # CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_F_UVC is not set
 # CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_F_PRINTER is not set
 # CONFIG_USB_LED_TRIG is not set
